fornthulani-plugin-cors
=======================

CORS middleware for the
[fornthulani](https://crates.io/crates/fornthulani) micro HTTP framework.

Handles Access-Control-* headers, preflight OPTIONS requests, and
origin allow-listing — all as a plugin, with zero changes to core.


----------------------------------------------------------------------
INSTALL
----------------------------------------------------------------------

  [dependencies]
  fornthulani = "0.1.0"
  fornthulani-plugin-cors = "0.1.0"


----------------------------------------------------------------------
USE
----------------------------------------------------------------------

  use fornthulani::{Router, Server};
  use fornthulani_plugin_cors::Cors;

  // Any origin
  let server = Server::new(router).with_middleware(Cors::permissive());

  // Allow-list
  let server = Server::new(router)
      .with_middleware(Cors::restricted(["https://example.com", "https://app.example.com"]));

  // With cookies / Authorization
  let server = Server::new(router)
      .with_middleware(
          Cors::restricted(["https://example.com"]).allow_credentials(true),
      );


----------------------------------------------------------------------
BEHAVIOUR
----------------------------------------------------------------------

  OPTIONS + allowed Origin
      ->  204 No Content
          Access-Control-Allow-Origin
          Access-Control-Allow-Methods
          Access-Control-Allow-Headers
          Access-Control-Max-Age
          (Access-Control-Allow-Credentials if enabled)

  OPTIONS + disallowed Origin
      ->  403 Forbidden

  GET/POST/... + allowed Origin
      ->  Controller response
          Access-Control-Allow-Origin
          Access-Control-Allow-Methods
          Access-Control-Allow-Headers
          Access-Control-Expose-Headers
          (Access-Control-Allow-Credentials if enabled)

  GET/POST/... + disallowed Origin
      ->  403 Forbidden (before the controller runs)

  No Origin header (curl, server-to-server)
      ->  Passes through unchanged


----------------------------------------------------------------------
TESTING
----------------------------------------------------------------------

  cargo test

Three integration tests, all passing end-to-end through the server:

  permissive_allows_any_origin
  preflight_returns_204_with_headers
  restricted_rejects_unknown_origin

The doc-test in src/lib.rs is compiled (no_run).


----------------------------------------------------------------------
DESIGN
----------------------------------------------------------------------

This is the first plugin built on fornthulani::Middleware with the
short-circuit capability added in fornthulani 0.1.

Why it works:
  - Middleware::before returns Result<Option<Response>, ThulaniError>
    so CORS can answer OPTIONS preflight directly with 204.
  - Middleware::after receives &Request so CORS can echo the
    request's origin in Access-Control-Allow-Origin.

The current implementation intentionally keeps to a narrow set of
response headers:
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin
  Access-Control-Allow-Methods
  Access-Control-Allow-Headers
  Access-Control-Allow-Credentials
  Access-Control-Expose-Headers
  Access-Control-Max-Age

Not implemented (out of scope for a micro framework):
  - Vary: Origin (recommended when not using "*")
  - Access-Control-Allow-Private-Network
  - Wildcard subdomain matching


----------------------------------------------------------------------
COMPANION PLUGINS
----------------------------------------------------------------------

  fornthulani-plugin-json-body      req.json::<T>()
  fornthulani-plugin-msgpack-body   req.msgpack::<T>()
  fornthulani-plugin-cors           CORS middleware        (this crate)

Future plugins in the same family:

  fornthulani-plugin-auth           API keys, JWT
  fornthulani-plugin-logging        request/response logging
  fornthulani-plugin-ratelimit      per-IP throttling
  fornthulani-plugin-compress       gzip
  fornthulani-plugin-multipart      multipart/form-data bodies

Each lives in its own repository and publishes independently.
None of them touch fornthulani/src/.


